  "text": "Current clinical trials | College of Veterinary Medicine\nSkip to main content\nGo to the University of Minnesota Twin Cities home page\nOne Stop\nMyU\nSearch\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nHospitals & care\nCurrent students\nMenu\nAbout us\nAbout\nInclusive Excellence\nInclusive excellence overview\nCommitment to inclusive excellence\nDiversity, Equity and Inclusion committee\nCommunity\nResources\nReporting bias or sexual misconduct\nInclusive Excellence Symposium\nEmployment\nOur faculty & staff\nStrategic plan 2023-2026\nImpact report\nEducation\nWhat we offer\nDoctor of Veterinary Medicine\nGraduate Programs\nDual degree programs\nDVM/MPH\nInternship & Residency Programs\nAccreditation\nDepartments\nDepartments overview\nDepartment of Veterinary and Biomedical Sciences\nVeterinary Clinical Sciences\nVeterinary Population Medicine\nDepartment of Veterinary Population Medicine\nOur faculty & staff\nResearch\nContact us\nTeaching\nSTEMMA\nCenters and programs\nCenters & programs overview\nCenter for Animal Health and Food Safety\nCanine Brain Tumor Program\nClinical Investigation Center\nCommunity medicine initiative\nJohn Fetrow Dairy Education center\nLeatherdale Equine Center\nMinnesota Urolith Center\nSecure Food Systems\nSecure Poultry Supply\nSwine program\nThe Raptor Center\nVeterinary Diagnostic Laboratory\nResearch\nResearch overview\nResearch news\nResearch office\nRIDE Summit\nRIDE Seminar Series\nAnimal Cancer Care & Research\nResearch labs\nResearch laboratories home\nBlood and Laboratory Support Services\nCanine genetics lab\nClinical Pathology Lab\nEquine Genetics and Genomics\nMinnesota Center for Prion Research and Outreach (MNPRO)\nMinnesota Urolith Center\nModiano Lab\nMycoplasma Research Laboratory\nResearch training programs\nNews & Events\nMedia Room\nProfiles\nEvents\nAlumni & Giving\nGive\nAlumni\nContact us\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nDepartments\nCenters and programs\nClinical Investigation Center\nCurrent clinical trials\nMain navigation\nClinical Investigation Center\nCurrent clinical trials\nExpand Current clinical trials menu\nCanine Brain Tumor Program\nCompleted clinical studies\nFor investigators\nExpand For investigators menu\nFor UMN & external collaborators\nFor CVM investigators\nAbout\nExpand About menu\nOur Staff\nContact us\nRegulatory information\nCurrent clinical trials\nWe have many opportunities for pet animals to participate in clinical trials. Each listing below has a quick summary plus a link to more information for each study.\nStatus\nOn hold\nOngoing but enrollment closed\nOpen and enrolling\nCategory\nAnesthesia and pain management\nCancer/Oncology\nCardiology\nDentistry and oral surgery\nDermatology\nGenetics\nInternal medicine\nNeurology\nOrthopedics/Surgery\nSpecies\nCat\nDog\nHorse\nAMPs:  canine pyoderma topical treatment study\nA canine clinical trial to test the efficacy and safety of superficial pyoderma using a ceragnin-based hydrogel.\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nDermatology\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nCanine Brain Tumor Program\nLeading edge research combined with compassionate care\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nNeurology\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nCAR-T cell therapy for canine CD20+ B cell lymphoma\nA canine clinical trial designed to evaluate the safety and efficacy of intranodal injection of a CAR-T product for the treatment of CD20+ B-cell lymphoma\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nOn hold\nCOED part 1 - dogs with Osteosarcoma ages 2-4\nBlood sampling study of dogs to develop test for early detection of canine osteosarcoma.\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nOngoing but enrollment closed\nCOED part 2 - canine Osteosarcoma\nStudy to develop a reliable, minimally-invasive blood test for early detection of canine osteosarcoma.\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nOngoing but enrollment closed\nFEHI - Feline SEHI for OA\nStudy for cats with radiographic evidence of osteoarthritis using a novel painkiller\nSpecies\nCat\nCategory\nAnesthesia and pain management\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nGenetic muscle diseases in horses\nSpecies\nHorse\nCategory\nGenetics\nInternal medicine\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nLyra 1 - blood collection study for lymphoma\nA minimally invasive blood sampling study to identify dogs at high risk of developing Diffuse Large B-cell Lymphoma (DLBCL).\nSamples must be collected at the University of Minnesota, Small Animal Hospital.\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nOngoing but enrollment closed\nLYRA 3 - blood collection study for lymphoma in healthy dogs at least 5 years old\nThis project aims to create a simple blood test that can accurately check if a healthy dog has undetected diffuse large b-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) or is at high risk of developing it. In the future, this test could be paired with targeted treatments to prevent tumors from developing.\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nNew vaccine for dogs with oral melanoma\nNovel adeno-associated virus (AAV) vaccine for dogs with malignant oral melanoma\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nOlaparib + Meloxicam for Feline Mammary Carcinoma\nA pilot clinical trial to evaluate the safety and efficacy of combination olaparib and meloxicam therapy for treatment of feline mammary carcinoma\nSpecies\nCat\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nORBIT - VSV and an anti-PD-1 inhibitor for Canine Lymphoma\nThis study hopes to understand how a\nnew combination immunotherapy\nworks and to determine if it is effective in the treatment for dogs with relapsed and refractory aggressive lymphoma.\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nPuppy Gait Analysis Study\nA canine clinical trial to evaluate gait development and coordination in puppies into adulthood.\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nOrthopedics/Surgery\nCurrent Status\nOpen and enrolling\nShine On Continuation\nStudy for dogs to test eBAT prevention of cancer\nSpecies\nDog\nCategory\nCancer/Oncology\nCurrent Status\nCompleted\nGlobal footer\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\n612-624-6244\nFax: 612-624-8753\n1365 Gortner Avenue\nSt. Paul, MN, 55108\nResources\nAlumni\nCampus maps\nContact us\nCurrent students\nEmployment\nIntranets\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nVeterinary Medical Center\nFeedback\nWebsite feedback\nGive\nFollow us\nResearch ethics at the University of Minnesota\n. We are committed to protecting research participants, upholding ethical standards, and improving our practice at every step of our work.\nFor Students, Faculty, and Staff\nOne Stop\nMyU\n©\n2026\nRegents of the\nUniversity of Minnesota\n. All rights reserved. The University of Minnesota is an equal opportunity educator and employer.\nPrivacy Statement\nReport Web Accessibility Issues\nAbout us\nAbout\nInclusive Excellence\nInclusive excellence overview\nCommitment to inclusive excellence\nDiversity, Equity and Inclusion committee\nCommunity\nResources\nReporting bias or sexual misconduct\nInclusive Excellence Symposium\nEmployment\nOur faculty & staff\nStrategic plan 2023-2026\nImpact report\nEducation\nWhat we offer\nDoctor of Veterinary Medicine\nGraduate Programs\nDual degree programs\nDVM/MPH\nInternship & Residency Programs\nAccreditation\nDepartments\nDepartments overview\nDepartment of Veterinary and Biomedical Sciences\nVeterinary Clinical Sciences\nVeterinary Population Medicine\nDepartment of Veterinary Population Medicine\nOur faculty & staff\nResearch\nContact us\nTeaching\nSTEMMA\nCenters and programs\nCenters & programs overview\nCenter for Animal Health and Food Safety\nCanine Brain Tumor Program\nClinical Investigation Center\nCurrent clinical trials\nCanine Brain Tumor Program\nCompleted clinical studies\nFor investigators\nFor UMN & external collaborators\nFor CVM investigators\nAbout\nOur Staff\nContact us\nRegulatory info